<%- include("layouts/headers") %>

<div class="container py-3">
  <h1>Shows loading during request</h1>
  <p>Below is an example of loading when making a request that may take a long time. The flow is as follows: when the request is made, intercept it with the before-request event and remove the d-none class to make the spinner appear. Then, after the request is complete, intercept it again with the after-request event and add the d-none class again to hide the loading again. The logic is in the script.js file in the public folder.</p>
  
  <form data-ajax
    data-swap="result"
    id="form"
    action="/partials/loading"
    method="get"
  >
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Greet</button>
  </form>
  
  <!-- spinner -->
  <div id="spinner" class="d-none vh-100 w-100 position-fixed top-0 start-0 d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center bg-dark bg-opacity-50 text-white">
    <div class="spinner-border text-warning" role="status">
      <span class="visually-hidden">Loading...</span>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<%- include("layouts/footers") %>